      <p class="eyebrow text-accent">Ristra Courts, 1948</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.5rem,3vw+1rem,4rem)] leading-[1.04]">Twelve motel rooms. Twelve rooms of music.</h1>
      <p class="body-copy mt-6 max-w-[50ch]">Ristra Courts opened on Route 66 in 1948: twelve single-story rooms around a gravel courtyard, with a carport for the Buicks. The last guest checked out in 2009. Seven years later Marisol Archuleta and Ray Gallegos, who had been teaching in their kitchens, asked the owner what one room would cost, and were given the keys to all twelve.</p>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4 max-w-[50ch]">Every room still has its number on the door. They rewired, plastered, hung doors thick enough to keep the trumpets in, and walled up the carport. They kept the sign. It says RISTRA COURTS, as it always has, with MUSIC LESSONS hung under it.</p>
